Back about 1990, a net vandal named Dave Hayes
led a cohort of similarly minded idiots, who
objected to moderated newsgroups, claiming that
the U.S. Constitution's "Freedom of Speech"
protection meant that that cohort had an absolute
right to "post whatever we want wherever we want",
ignoring that the entire purpose of newsgroups
was to create arenas for _focused_ discussions.

This cohort proceeded to forge (sometimes hundreds
of) off-topic postings to moderated newsgroups,
adding bogus moderator approval signatures.

At that point I began trying to make the point by
example that Usenet _already has_ a "post whatever
you want" newgroup, misc.misc, and that this cohort
should move their discussions there, and leave the
moderated newsgroups in peace.

I don't think my crossposting everything in the
dozens of newsgroups to which I contribute into
misc.misc ever had the slightest impact on the
cohort of vandals, but by now it has become a
habit. Besides which, there are at least two "fans"
of mine who read misc.misc strictly to follow all
of my output, so in some sense I owe them the grace
of continuing to crosspost all I can remember to
do.

